@auth.sigil from Auth import { identity and access, room owner }

component ResourceManagement {
    goal {
        Manages *Room* and *room metadata*, and defines *base availability rules*,
        so room owners can publish spaces and Booking can check a
        *requested time range* against those rules.
    }

    interface {
        A Room has a *resource identifier*, room metadata including display name,
        location, capacity, and optional amenities.

        A room owner can create a Room, update its metadata, publish it for search,
        or archive it.

        A Room's base availability rules describe recurring open periods and
        date-specific closures.

        Given a Room and a requested period, Resource Management returns a
        *room availability answer* stating whether the entire period fits its
        applicable base availability rules.

        Room search returns available Room values matching a supplied location and
        minimum capacity.
    }

    state {
        Resource Management owns Room, room metadata, and base availability rules.

        A Room can be draft, available, unavailable, or archived.
    }

    logic {
        A room owner publishes a draft Room with base availability rules to make it
        available for search.

        An available Room appears in search only when it matches every supplied
        filter.

        A room availability answer is available only when the Room is available,
        the full requested time range falls within open periods, and it does not
        overlap an applicable closure.

        A room availability answer is unavailable when the Room is unavailable, any
        part of the range falls outside an open period, or the range overlaps an
        applicable closure.
    }

    constraints {
        identity and access supplies current-user and permission checks;
        Resource Management does not own users, sessions, roles, or permission policy.

        Resource Management's base availability rules answer does not include
        booking-conflict checks, which Booking owns.

        Recurring open periods in base availability rules remain owned by Resource
        Management, while Scheduling and Recurrence owns recurring patterns, series,
        and exceptions.
    }

    cases {
        A room owner publishes a Room with open periods and a date-specific closure.

        Booking asks whether a requested range fits a Room's base availability rules
        and receives an available or unavailable answer.
    }
}
